From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: build the torchtext libraries as C++20

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [torchtext development stopped after 0.18.0; only needed to build it against a libtorch newer than the 2.3 it was released for]

libtorch 2.14 refuses to compile as anything older than C++20
(ATen/ATen.h and torch/all.h #error out, and c10/util/intrusive_ptr.h
uses std::strong_ordering), while torchtext hardcodes
CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17. Raising the global standard is not enough on its
own: the vendored re2 does not build as C++20 (walker-inl.h declares its
constructor as WalkState<T>(...), a template-id the C++20 grammar
rejects). Switch to C++20 only after third_party/ has been added, so
libtorchtext and _torchtext follow libtorch while the static third-party
libraries keep building as C++17.

Reproduces on any architecture against libtorch 2.14.
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index b789a32..3631444 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -64,4 +64,6 @@ endif()
 set(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS "${CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS} ${TORCH_COMPILED_WITH_CXX_ABI} -Wall ${TORCH_CXX_FLAGS}")
 
 add_subdirectory(third_party)
+# libtorch 2.14 headers require C++20; the bundled re2 does not build as C++20.
+set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 20)
 add_subdirectory(torchtext/csrc)
-- 
